 "text": "Webster County Nebraska\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nEmployment\nHistory\nHistorical Information\nVisitors Committee Grant App\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's\nOffice\nGIS Workshop\nSales Files\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary\nDischarge\nProperty Valuation\nProtests\nSpecial\nLicenses\nCounty Court\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict\nCourt Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's\nOffice\nElection Information\nLocal Election Results\nEmergency Manager\nExtension\nOffice\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of\nDeeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's\nOffice\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's\nExam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nOffice Services\nOther Organizations\nFeedback\n-->\nWelcome\nNebraska County Websites\nWebster County\nOur new website was brought online in May 2012\nwith the help of MIPS Inc. MIPS Inc is the Technology Services\nDivision of the Nebraska Association of County Officials (NACO).\nNACO's website address is\nnebraskacounties.org\nWebster Courthouse\nAddress\n621 N Cedar Street\nRed Cloud, NE 68970\nPhone\n402-746-2716\n(County Clerk)\nHours\n8:00 am - 4:00 pm\nLocation\nOur online forms and documents are in PDF format.\nIf you do not have the latest Adobe's PDF reader installed, click on\nthe Adobe PDF image below.\nPublic Notices\nMay 16, 2024 Press Release - 911 Calls\nWe invite you to browse our web site to learn about our various County\noffices and the services Webster County, Nebraska offers its citizens.\nCourthouse hours are from 8:00 - 4:00, Monday - Friday except on holidays.\nThis web site contains information about County programs, services,\ndepartments and offices, as well as helpful information on commonly\nasked questions. We encourage you to use this site frequently to access\nagendas and minutes of the Board of County Commissioners.\nThe Courthouse will be closed:\nMartin Luther King, Jr. Day\n|\nJanuary 19\nThird Monday in January\n|\nPresident's Day\n|\nFebruary 16\nThird Monday in February\n|\nArbor Day\n|\nApril 24\nLast Friday in April\n|\nMemorial Day\n|\nMay 25\nLast Monday in May\n|\nJuneteenth\n|\nJune 19\n|\nIndependence Day\n|\nJuly 4\n|\nLabor Day\n|\nSeptember 7\nFirst Monday in September\n|\nColumbus Day\n|\nOctober 12\nSecond Monday in October\n|\nVeteran's Day\n|\nNovember 11\n|\nThanksgiving Day\n|\nNovember 26\nFourth Thursday in November\n|\nDay after Thanksgiving\n|\nNovember 27\nFriday following Thanksgiving\n|\nChristmas\n|\nDecember 24 @ 12:00 p.m.\nDecember 25 |\nNew Years\n|\nJanuary 1, 2027\n|\nCopyright © 2012 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
